    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d963">

                <pb facs="1018" n="1006" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg1006"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/425: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-08-19">August 19,
                        1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>988. Your 1458, August 9, indicates that Soviet Government intends to observe on
                    the basis of reciprocity the Geneva Red Cross Convention of July 27, 1929. The
                    Department would appreciate being informed whether the Soviet Union also intends
                    to observe the prisoner of war convention signed at Geneva on the same
                        date<anchor n="48" xml:id="d963-f1"/> or the convention on that subject
                    signed on July 6, 1906.<anchor n="49" xml:id="d963-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d963-f1" n="48" xml:id="d963-f1-content">
                <p>For text, see <ref target="frus1929v01#pg_336">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1929, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 336</ref>; or League of Nations
                    Treaty Series, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">cxviii</hi>, p. 343.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d963-f2" n="49" xml:id="d963-f2-content">
                <p>International Red Cross Convention, for the Amelioration of the Condition of the
                    Wounded of the Armies in the Field, signed at Geneva; for text, see <ref
                        target="frus1906p2#pg_1559">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1906, pt. 2, p. 1559</ref>;
                    or 35 Stat. 1885.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
